{
  "name": "http-parser",
  "description": "A high-performance, zero-allocation HTTP message parser written in C, designed for use in streaming network applications. It implements a robust finite-state machine to handle requests and responses without performing system calls or internal buffering, supporting features like chunked transfer encoding and protocol upgrades. The library provides a callback-based interface for extracting headers, URLs, and message bodies with minimal memory overhead, typically requiring only 40 bytes per stream.",
